## J.2 `YMRowCScaleTimeHessianDebtIntegralGateExact.agda` — the temporal gate row C must pass

Every Balaban estimate is indexed by RG scale; the Heat/Doob debt is an integral
in heat time, and with block size `L` the `j`-th scale occupies a time interval
of width `w_j = w₀ τ^j`, `τ = L²`. Since the debt is constant on each interval,
its integral is *exactly* the finite sum `Σ w_j η_j`, so the question is exact
rational arithmetic:

* `dilatedDebtBudget` — `η_j ≤ E₀ ρ^j` and `w_j = w₀ τ^j` give a bound on every
  prefix, at every starting scale, by any `B` closing `w₀E₀ + (ρτ)B ≤ B`. This
  requires `ρτ < 1`, i.e. `ρ < L⁻²`.
* `squaredRateDebtBudget` — at the squared rate `η_j ≤ D₀ (ρ²)^j` the gate
  relaxes to `ρ²τ < 1`, i.e. `ρ < L⁻¹`.
* `undilatedDebtHasFloor`, `debtFloorCapsScaleWindow` — the converse and the
  falsifiability clause: if the per-scale debt does not beat the dilation, the
  integrand has a positive floor, and any claimed uniform budget `B` caps the
  number of contributing scales by `B/c`. No better constant repairs it.
* The `L = 2` arithmetic is checked on both sides: `linearRateGateFailsAtL2`
  (`ρ = 1/3` gives `ρτ = 4/3 ≥ 1`) against `squaredRateBudgetAtL2`
  (`ρ²τ = 4/9`, explicit budget `2`).

*Still input:* the same-density identification — that the discrete-RG Hessian
data at scale `j` is a Hessian floor for the literal Heat/Doob `V_t` of the same
Gibbs density on the `j`-th interval — and cutoff/volume-uniform values of
`w₀, E₀, ρ, τ`.

